      "content": "Typically, it's about $189 and packing supplies for a one bedroom apartment pack but it's gonna be quite a bit less than that for, for this cause there's no close it's probably gonna be more along the lines of like maybe $50 or $60 and like boxes paper tape to kind of get the kitchen packed up. You only pay for the supplies we actually use but, yeah, everything else is included, there's no trip fees, there's no taxes, there's no credit card fees. We pad and wrap all the furniture that's included insurance on all the items as well as disassemble reassembly with the tools that we have on-hand and then the way that it works is we do a two and a half hour minimum. Once we exceed the minimum we bill in fifteen minute increments until the move is completed so you just pay for the time use. So the, yeah, the base minimum is $550 and then once we go over the two and a half hour market's fifteen minute increments of billing but a one bedroom apartment move typically takes two guys around two and a half to three and a half hours and then packing usually takes about the same but I would put your packing.",
